{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Whoever touches a dead body.</b> And which dead body? That of a human soul — to exclude the soul of an animal, whose impurity does not require sprinkling. Another interpretation: <b>a soul</b> — this is a quarter-log of blood (Ḥulin 72a)." "<b>He has defiled the Tabernacle of YHWH.</b> If he entered the courtyard even after immersion, without the sprinkling of the third and seventh day." "<b>His impurity is still upon him</b> — even though he immersed."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:37.789194432Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}